                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3804334774"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Does this change really solve anything? Integer division rounds down, so if `!tui->stopped && !tui->input.read_stream.did_eof)`, `LOOP_PROCESS_EVENTS_UNTIL()` should have waited for longer the needed timeout (as it rounds down multiple times in `remaining -= (int64_t)((now - before) / 1000000);`), not shorter.",
            "commit_id": "6234b2b36ba430280d36581f145de1c78ff04031",
            "created_at": "2026-08-18T13:10:12Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -765,9 +766,10 @@ void tui_stop(TUIData *tui)\n   terminfo_disable(tui);\n \n   // Wait until DA1 response is received, or stdin is closed (#35744).\n+  uint64_t wait_start = os_hrtime();\n   LOOP_PROCESS_EVENTS_UNTIL(tui->loop, tui->loop->events, EXIT_TIMEOUT_MS,\n                             tui->stopped || tui->input.read_stream.did_eof);\n-  if (!tui->stopped && !tui->input.read_stream.did_eof) {\n+  if (!tui->stopped && (os_hrtime() - wait_start) / 1000000 >= EXIT_TIMEOUT_MS) {",
